{"ticker":"LAURUSLABS","symbol":"LAURUSLABS","instrumentId":3141452,"name":"Laurus Labs","industry":"NSE-Medical-Diversified","about":"Laurus Labs Ltd. is a research-driven pharmaceutical manufacturing company known for its expertise in Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients (APIs) and intermediates, particularly in the areas of anti-retrovirals, oncology, cardiovascular, and gastro therapeutics. Since its inception in 2005, Laurus Labs has grown to become a trusted global leader in the pharmaceutical value chain, offering Contract Development and Manufacturing (CDMO) services for both generics and proprietary products. The company is also expanding into biotechnology through its Laurus Bio division, focusing on cell and gene therapies. Laurus Labs is committed to sustainability and regulatory compliance, ensuring transparency, integrity, and excellence across its operations worldwide.","website":"www.lauruslabs.com","location":"India","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:37:46.315Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":2306,"changePct":-0.7104413347685684,"week52High":2454,"week52Low":944.9},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹1,24,596 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹7,823 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"394,427,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"813"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"230,696,271"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.10%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"23.49"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.3"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"12.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.36"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.88"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-4%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"92.91"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"25–213"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"16.8%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"30.07"},{"label":"Volume","value":"842,779"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"2,190,831"},{"label":"Master score","value":"85"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"67"},{"label":"Price strength","valu